# Build output. `target/` rather than the three rooted paths this replaces:
# the repository holds three crates side by side, each with its own, and a
# rule listing them by name misses every crate added after it was written.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Firmware images and stray binaries. The RP2040 crates emit these beside the
# crate when an image is converted or flashed by hand, and none of them is
# source. `memory.x` is a linker script, is tracked, and is not matched here.
*.uf2
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
a.out
*.exe
*.so
*.dylib
*.o
core

# The tooling this happens to be written with. None of it describes the bus
# spec, all of it changes every session, and a repository is better for not
# carrying somebody else's editor state.
.claude/
.claude-flow/
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
/memory/
/coordination/
.swarm/
.hive-mind/
.roo/
.roomodes

# The house rules the code is written to: kept out of the published tree on
# purpose, so anyone reading the repository is reading the spec.
instructions.md
